{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Before they lay down.</b> And it does not say ״after they ate and the men of,״ etc. — this tells that there were matters between them in the meantime, namely the merit of those men, their memory for blessing (Genesis Rabbah 50:5), that Lot was a good intercessor on behalf of Sodom. And the reason Sodom was not overturned then, immediately, I have already explained (Genesis 18:21): because they were still in doubt of salvation, as it says ״אֵרְדָה נָּא וְאֶרְאֶה.״ And so too our Sages said in the Midrash (Genesis Rabbah 50:5), and this is their language: Lot was seeking mercy for Sodom and they were accepting from him, but once they said ״הוֹצִיאֵם וְגוֹ׳ וְנֵדְעָה״ etc., they said to him ״עוֹד״ etc. Another reason they did not destroy Sodom at that hour: they waited until daybreak so that it would be the special time of mercy to save Lot, whereas at night, when the judgments prevail, Lot would not escape. And our Sages, their memory for blessing, said (Genesis Rabbah 50:5): because they worshipped the sun and the moon, He smote them before the eyes of the sun and the moon on the sixteenth of Nisan."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:22.798920651Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}